            "review_title": "Review at Pho Ong Ca",
            "review_text": "Quang Pham\n9 contributions\n0\nTruly authentic Northern \"phở\" flavor\nDec 2016 • Family\nthe origin of Phở is from the North, said to be Nam Định province. This is a small shop, owned by a lady coming from Nam Định. It seems that her family has cooked phở for 4 consecutive generations. I rarely eat phở in HCMC but only in Hanoi. When i tried this restaurant, i was really surprised. Often took two bowls of phở whenever i came. Their specialty is \"phở đuôi bò\" (ox tail) but my preference is \"phở tái băm\" (minced rare beef with ginger). Pricing is cheap, only $1.5 per bowl (feel full). Strongly recommend!\nRead more\nValue\nService\nFood\nReview collected in partnership with this restaurant \nWritten February 2, 2017",
